# Every image builds with the repository root as its context (compose.yaml; `docker build -f
# apps/server/Dockerfile .`), so this is the only .dockerignore Docker reads. The site image runs
# `COPY . .`: anything not listed here lands in its build stage and the layer cache.

# Secrets and local data: no build reads them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.docker.example
.private
load-testing

# Dependencies and build output: each image installs and builds its own.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.source
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/build
**/dist
**/out
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.lighthouse
**/npm-debug.log

# Repository, editor and agent files.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.dockerignore
**/.vscode
**/.vs
**/.idea
.github
.claude
.agents
.gemini
.hallmark
apps/*/audit

# Container files.
**/Dockerfile*
**/docker-compose*
**/compose.y*ml

LICENSE
README.md
